# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for barch.
#
# Use with:
#   TSAN_OPTIONS="suppressions=ci/tsan.supp" ...
#
# See DONE 189 for how the one entry below was arrived at, and ci/README.md
# for the rest of the TSan recipe (the runtime has to be preloaded, and ASLR
# turned off with setarch -R, because _barch.so is dlopened by python).

# TSan does not intercept pthread_mutex_timedlock, so it never sees a lock
# taken through std::timed_mutex::try_lock_for(). Every later unlock of that
# mutex then looks unbalanced and is reported as "unlock of an unlocked mutex
# (or by a wrong thread)".
#
# barch takes its write latch that way on the main path -
# abstract_shard::lock_unique() is try_lock_for(lock_to_ms) - so this fires
# once per write unlock: 1042 reports in one chaos run against 114 real ones,
# which buries anything worth reading.
#
# It is a sanitizer limitation, not a barch defect. That was settled two ways:
# a twelve line program with no barch in it reproduces the report exactly, and
# an owner-tracking probe wrapped around every acquisition path of
# upgrade_write_mtx found no unbalanced or cross-thread unlock across a 347
# shard load and a full chaos run.
#
# The cost of this entry is that a genuine unbalanced unlock inside
# debuggable_server_lock would also be hidden. Take it out and use the owner
# probe from DONE 189 if that is ever in question.
mutex:debuggable_server_lock::unlock

# The lock's own diagnostics, not barch. capture_writer_stack() fills
# diags.writer_frames with backtrace() while a timeout dump could be reading it,
# and note_writer() sets the thread id and timestamp beside it. Racy, and it
# does not matter: it is a best-effort snapshot for a log line.
#
# It is also not in a release build. This whole block is behind
# BARCH_LOCK_DEBUG, which CMakeLists turns on for Debug and RelWithDebInfo -
# and RelWithDebInfo is what a sanitizer build uses. So this is a race in the
# instrumentation rather than in the thing being instrumented. 13 reports in
# one short-set run. See DONE 203 and TODO 213.
race:debuggable_server_lock::capture_writer_stack
race:debuggable_server_lock::note_writer
race:debuggable_server_lock::append_writer_stack
